<report>
<title>ROC Curve Analysis</title>
<line><in>chart</in></line>
<line></line>
<block name="datasets">
<line>Data set: <in>ti</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Area under ROC curve by extended trapezoidal rule = <in>auc</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Wilcoxon estimate of area under ROC curve = <in>theta</in></line>
<line>DeLong standard error = <in>se</in>:  <ci><in>pc</in>% CI = <in>ll</in> to <in>ul</in></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line>Optimum cut-off point selected = <in>cut</in></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><td><ci>Table at cut-off:</ci></td><td>a</td><td>b</td></tr>
<tr><td></td><td><in>a</in></td><td><in>b</in></td></tr>
<tr><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td></td><td>c</td><td>d</td></tr>
<tr><td></td><td><in>c</in></td><td><in>d</in></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line></line>
<line><b>Predictive value of +ve test </b>(post-test likelihood of disease)</line>
<line><in>likely</in> <ci>(<in>likely_from</in> to <in>likely_to</in>)</ci>, <in>likely_pc</in>% <ci>(<in>likely_from_pc</in>% to <in>likely_to_pc</in>%)</ci>,  {change = <in>likely_change</in>%}</line>
<line></line>
<line><b>Predictive values of -ve test</b></line>
<line>(post-test likelihood of no disease)</line>
<line><in>likely_negative</in> <ci>(<in>likely_negative_from</in> to <in>likely_negative_to</in>)</ci>, <in>likely_negative_pc</in>% <ci>(<in>likely_negative_from_pc</in>% to <in>likely_negative_to_pc</in>%)</ci>,  {change = <in>likely_negative_change</in>%}</line>
<line>(post-test disease likelihood despite -ve test)</line>
<line><in>likely_despite</in> <ci>(<in>likely_despite_from</in> to <in>likely_despite_to</in>)</ci>, <in>likely_despite_pc</in>% <ci>(<in>likely_despite_from_pc</in>% to <in>likely_despite_to_pc</in>%)</ci>, {change = <in>likely_despite_change</in>%}</line>
<line></line>
<line>sensitivity (<in>senspc</in>% CI) = <in>sens</in>  (<in>sensll</in> to <in>sensul</in>)</line>
<line><ci>specificity (<in>specpc</in>% CI) = <in>spec</in>  (<in>specll</in> to <in>specul</in>)</ci></line>
</block>
</report>
